    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39009" root="موت" body-key="m">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَيْتٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَيِّتٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَرْضٌ مَيْتَةٌ</span>: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَوَاتٌ</span>:
<i>Unfruitful land;</i> like as <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ارض حَيَّةٌ</span> means fruitful
land, or land abounding with herbage. (TA, in
art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حى</span>.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَيْتَةٌ</span> <i>Carrion:</i> whatsoever hath not
been killed in the manner prescribed by the law.
(K, Jel, ii. 168.) See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَيِّتٌ</span>.

